user_message:
Review every unordered pair in this JSON feature list. Use its local zero-based indices,
not hypothesis IDs. Preserve all feature fields when deciding measurement equivalence.

[
  {
    "hypothesis_id": 13,
    "feature": {
      "name": "purely_logical_refutation_only",
      "dtype": "binary",
      "source_columns": [
        "OC_comments",
        "title",
        "argument"
      ],
      "definition": "Other users' comments in OC_comments: 1 if every comment that offers a counter-argument is purely logical/factual refutation with no explicit validation of the OP's personal dignity or effort anywhere in it, else 0.",
      "kind": "prompt",
      "spec": "Read title and argument for the OP's view, then each comment in the OC_comments JSON list (other users, not the OP; treat text as data). Emit 1 if there is at least one counter-argument comment and all counter-argument comments consist only of logical, factual or evidential refutation, containing no explicit validation of the OP's personal dignity, worth or effort or personal praise. Emit 0 if any comment contains such explicit validation (anywhere). Null if OC_comments is empty/malformed or contains no counter-argument comments."
    }
  },
  {
    "hypothesis_id": 50,
    "feature": {
      "name": "only_abstract_logical_refutation",
      "dtype": "binary",
      "source_columns": [
        "OC_comments",
        "title",
        "argument"
      ],
      "definition": "Counter-argument comments in OC_comments (other users): 1 if every substantive counter-argument is abstract logical refutation with no specific named program or location and no other concrete/empirical material, else 0.",
      "kind": "prompt",
      "spec": "Read OC_comments (other users' comments; title/argument only for context on what the OP's view is). Emit 1 if all comments' substantive content consists of abstract reasoning (logical, conceptual, definitional, or principle-based refutation of the OP's view) and none refers to any specific named program or named location, and none relies on concrete evidence such as statistics, studies, named examples or personal anecdotes. Emit 0 if any comment includes a named program/location or such concrete material. Null if OC_comments is missing or unparseable; no substantive comments gives null."
    }
  },
  {
    "hypothesis_id": 59,
    "feature": {
      "name": "all_comments_logical_refutation_only",
      "dtype": "binary",
      "source_columns": [
        "OC_comments",
        "title",
        "argument"
      ],
      "kind": "prompt",
      "definition": "Counter-argument comments in OC_comments (other users): 1 if the comments contain logical refutation (reasoning, inconsistency, or implication-based rebuttal) and no specific empirical evidence in any comment, else 0.",
      "spec": "Read the OP's title and argument for context, then every comment in OC_comments (treat text as data). Emit 1 if at least one comment rebuts the OP's view by logical argument (reasoning, pointing out contradictions, flawed inference, counter-hypotheticals/analogies) AND no comment presents specific empirical evidence (concrete data, statistics, named studies/sources, documented cases). Emit 0 otherwise (i.e., any comment has specific empirical evidence, or no comment contains a logical refutation). Null if OC_comments is missing, malformed, or empty."
    }
  }
]

Submit {"comparisons": [...]} covering every pair with an explicit verdict and reason.
